          "text": "1. Debt-funded extraction limits retained creditor cushion — Analyst Interpretation; Material risk. CP-1A BF01/GT01/GT02 and CP-1 BS14 establish borrowing linked to a non-earning equity payout and a substantial accrued payment. The mechanism leaves debt service behind while removing cash, restricting the inference from gross base-date liquidity and elevating future capital-allocation monitoring. No FY2024/FY2023 buybacks, explicit reporting and historical extensions are credible contrary evidence, not reversal of the dividend. Sustained retention, restrained distributions and evidenced debt reduction would improve the view; further debt-funded shareholder returns would weaken it.",
