              "locator": "line 89",
              "quote": "**Definitions change capacity, not just reported leverage.** L p.5 L410–L424 defines FCCR as legal EBITDA over Fixed Charges for four full quarters with internal statements, pro forma financing and acquisitions/dispositions, transaction-date floating rates and swap effects. Fixed Charges adds tax-grossed preferred dividends to defined interest. Defined interest excludes financing-fee amortization, bridge/commitment fees, qualified securitization costs and prepayment premiums, while adding capitalized interest and capital-lease interest. EBITDA includes expansive transaction, restructuring, dividend-equivalent and projected-savings adjustments. Clause M's 35% limit is neither a global cap on all EBITDA add-backs nor a cap on every pro forma acquisition adjustment: L421–L422 separately permits officer-good-faith acquisition calculations and reasonably determined operating expense reductions. The no-duplication and specified exclusions still matter; the document is not permission to add the same amount twice. Wider earnings and narrower fixed charges can make ratio debt and distributions easier before actual cash savings arrive, increasing debt-service sensitivity and weakening the residual asset cushion. Monitor adjustment categories, actual realization and transaction-date rate inputs, not the accounting multiple."
            }
