          "table_id": "prose-CP-4-6",
          "row_id": "r1",
          "field": "c0",
          "amount": null,
          "text": "Debt and lien permissions are separate. L p.18 §4.09 L1295 says “greater than 2.0 to 1.0”, not greater than or equal. L p.10 L715 says “shall not exceed 5.25 to 1.00” for the specific (xxxi) Ratio Indebtedness lien route. Permitted Liens (iii) covers Bank Indebtedness; (xx) links purchase-money and additional-debt baskets to asset-specific/collateral-only limits; (xxi) confines foreign-sub liens to foreign-sub assets. Accordingly, 5.25 is not a blanket secured leverage maintenance ceiling or a condition on every lien. Permitted-debt reclassification can refresh fixed baskets; acquisition debt can use an improved-FCCR alternative even without satisfying the USD1 ratio-debt test. These provisions can permit further pari claims or locally senior funding without a new breach, but actual priming is not established. The contrary case is §4.12's express junior-or-permitted requirement and §9.02's affected-holder ranking protection. A proposed priority change must satisfy those boundaries and the missing ICA, rather than relying on a generic majority-vote claim.",
