          "row_id": "r7",
          "field": "c0",
          "amount": null,
          "text": "LME/control protection is mixed rather than absent. §9.02 expressly contemplates consents in tender/exchange offers; general covenant changes can bind dissenters by majority. However, affected-holder protections include principal, fixed maturity, redemption terms, interest/payment timing, currency, payment suit, adversely changed ranking and specified post-trigger change-of-control obligations. L p.27 L1857 protects changes “affecting the subordination or ranking of the Notes or the Guarantees” adverse to holders. A materially adverse ICA modification or unauthorized all/substantially all collateral release needs 66⅔%, not merely majority. §2.09 excludes issuer/control-affiliate votes, with trustee actual-knowledge protection. §6.06 prohibits using the indenture to obtain preference over another holder; §6.07 preserves individual due-payment suits. These are meaningful opposite-case barriers. They do not prove that every non-pro-rata exchange, open-market purchase or asset-based transaction is prohibited, or that a majority can validly override every priority right. No executed coercive LME, uptier or drop-down is established by the supplied actions.",
