          "text": "Time-aware downside: an aerospace utilization/supply shock in CP-2 first reduces deliverable shipments or mix, then cash collection and legal earnings. There is no automatic numerical notes-maintenance breach solely because EBITDA falls. New incurrence/RP ability may tighten at transaction dates, while previously compliant contractual RP commitments may still drain cash; LCA tests may already have been locked at signing. If refinancing/receivables liquidity becomes insufficient, a missed payment, cross-final-maturity failure or acceleration can engage Article VI after its actual notice/grace rules. Enforcement then moves through agents and the missing ICA, with permitted releases and competing liens determining reachable value. Observable triggers are transaction certificates, commitment dates, liquidity events, formal notices, collateral releases and agent directions—not an invented covenant breach date or forecast.",
