          "text": "For the 6.000% 2033 secured notes only, L p.15 §3.07 reports ordinary calls at 103.000 in the twelve-month period beginning September 15, 2027, 101.500 in 2028 and 100.000 from 2029, plus accrued interest. Prior redemption uses applicable-premium terms; an equity-offering route permits up to 40% at 106.000 before September 15, 2027, with at least 60% remaining and specified 90-day/purpose conditions. Section 3.08 supplies no scheduled sinking fund and permits open-market purchases. These are contractual prices expressed as percent of principal, not market quotes or predicted exercises. Improved credit/rates may allow refinancing and cap bond price upside, while adverse conditions leave the holder exposed to longer duration. No YTW can be computed without price, complete cash-flow dates and exercise assumptions. None of this call schedule is attributed to the 2028–2032 notes or any 2033 instrument other than this supplied 6.000% series.",
