              "quote": "| B3: deferred term-loan/note bullets provide time | CP-1 F07 reports July 11, 2025 A/R maturity, 487 gross drawn and 650 capacity; BS14/SE03 shows committed cash uses before that renewal. S1 p.45 reports 67 LCs and 843 revolver availability, not unrestricted cash. | A conditional funding/collection need can precede the bond wall, particularly after cash extraction or under weaker eligible receivables. | CP-4 describes non-recourse securitization pool/undertakings and no recurring numerical notes-maintenance test; no note-maintenance trigger forces early deleveraging simply because earnings fall. | Tenor relief is useful but not proof the business can bridge earlier renewal or accessibility needs; operational cash and funding eligibility must coexist. | Negative — Refinancing Risk | Actual scope-matched renewal/funding evidence and a complete accessible liquidity bridge through commitments, amortization and stress. No renewal failure is asserted from missing follow-up. |"
