          "text": "Exactly one greatest uncertainty: the amount and durability of retained, accessible liquidity after committed uses. Reported base-date cash precedes October settlement, and consolidated cash does not identify entity-level access or required operating balances. This uncertainty determines whether operating interruption is absorbable or becomes funding dependence before bond maturities. Resolve it with a complete date-matched cash/funding bridge, cash location/restrictions, operating and integration needs, legal/facility draw conditions, eligible receivables, actual renewals and supported stress inputs. A positive resolution would let the committee reconsider a Watchlist or, only after independent pricing/legal/mandate gates, Starter Position; it would not automatically approve either. A negative resolution showing a substantiated unmanageable funding deficit would support Avoid for new risk, with any Reduce/Exit decision dependent on actual holdings, prices and alternatives. These are resolution impacts, not substitutes for today's selected posture.",
