          "cached_value": null,
          "hidden": false,
          "data_type": null,
          "number_format": null,
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "locator": "line 455",
          "text": "**Cash conversion.** CFO increased by 670 (K13; CF22); the complete source changes-in-assets/liabilities block remained a cash use, but its use narrowed by 129 (K03/K13). K12 conversion improved, and K02 CFO less capex increased. CF24 acquisitions and CF28 distributions are outside that FCF definition, so this does not establish cash available for debt paydown. Cash interest CF43 is distinct from IS07 and CB03, while tax paid CF44 is distinct from IS11; neither accrual earnings nor the issuer's EBITDA adjustment bridge is a substitute for cash flows. Source non-GAAP cautions explicitly identify interest, taxes, replacement expenditure and cash integration costs as omitted burdens (S1 p.52).",
          "formula": null,
          "cached_value": null,
          "hidden": false,
          "data_type": null,
          "number_format": null,
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "locator": "line 457",
          "text": "**Funding and leverage.** K07 carrying debt increased by 5,130 (K13), while reported cash CF42 increased and the cash-netted K10 multiple declined. Gross carrying leverage K09 nevertheless increased: the two directions are not contradictory because cash netting changes the numerator. The liquidity implication of that netting is restricted: BS14/SE01 identifies a declared payment obligation and SE03 records its October settlement. S1 p.131 explicitly says the fourth-quarter notes and term-loan proceeds, together with cash on hand, were used to fund the special-dividend declaration. S1 p.128 separately identifies 2031 notes/Tranche J proceeds and cash as financing the CPI Electron Device acquisition. These are documented funding links, not an inference from simultaneous debt and dividends. Reported positive financing CF38 supported the historical cash rollforward; no claim that all base-date cash was accessible, unrestricted or permanent is made.",
          "formula": null,
          "cached_value": null,
          "hidden": false,
          "data_type": null,
          "number_format": null,
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "locator": "line 459",
          "text": "**Coverage and quality.** Operating-income/net-interest coverage K11 improved, but it is an accounting ratio using net interest, not cash coverage or a covenant headroom test. EB06–EB09 include compensation, financing and acquisition-related adjustments across comparative periods; CP-1D must test recurrence and cash consequences rather than accepting their add-back status. S1 p.143 discloses liability-based awards and recurring measurement; S1 p.52 warns of cash integration cost exclusions. No independent adjusted earnings restatement is presented here.",
