        {
          "locator": "line 159",
          "text": "**Capacity versus willingness versus feasibility.** L tool pp.16–18 §4.07 L1202–L1277 defines restricted payments and conditions/exceptions; L1265 includes both no continuing default and a pro forma Consolidated Fixed Charge Coverage Ratio exceeding 2.0 to 1.0. L1272–L1274 contains continuing-obligation and classification/combination provisions. These are operative words requiring complete definitions and fact inputs, not a calculation using CP-1 K11. L tool p.16 §4.04 L1185–L1188 requires officers' compliance certificates; none is supplied. S1 p.132 states issuer covenant compliance; it is management's documentary assertion, not this module's compliance opinion. Willingness is demonstrated by BF01, not by the existence of §4.07. Feasibility is limited to historical issuance/payment actions; cash accessibility, remaining baskets and current market access remain unestablished. No statement that the September distribution relied on a particular basket is made.",
