          "number_format": null,
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "locator": "line 165",
          "text": "**Contrary evidence.** No FY2024/FY2023 buybacks under the program (S1 p.140); audited reporting and explicit non-GAAP caution (pp.103, 141); historical maturity extensions and spread reductions (pp.128–130); multiple product/customer/end-market exposures (pp.5–7). These temper a one-sided extraction narrative but do not reverse BF01's cash/debt mechanics. Conversely, government contract rights, OEM cyclicality, supplier requalification constraints and channel-mix sensitivity counter an unconditional aftermarket-resilience thesis. Supportive reporting does not offset an actual cash distribution, and absent support evidence is neither neutral nor adverse.",
