        {
          "locator": "line 89",
          "text": "**Definitions change capacity, not just reported leverage.** L p.5 L410–L424 defines FCCR as legal EBITDA over Fixed Charges for four full quarters with internal statements, pro forma financing and acquisitions/dispositions, transaction-date floating rates and swap effects. Fixed Charges adds tax-grossed preferred dividends to defined interest. Defined interest excludes financing-fee amortization, bridge/commitment fees, qualified securitization costs and prepayment premiums, while adding capitalized interest and capital-lease interest. EBITDA includes expansive transaction, restructuring, dividend-equivalent and projected-savings adjustments. Clause M's 35% limit is neither a global cap on all EBITDA add-backs nor a cap on every pro forma acquisition adjustment: L421–L422 separately permits officer-good-faith acquisition calculations and reasonably determined operating expense reductions. The no-duplication and specified exclusions still matter; the document is not permission to add the same amount twice. Wider earnings and narrower fixed charges can make ratio debt and distributions easier before actual cash savings arrive, increasing debt-service sensitivity and weakening the residual asset cushion. Monitor adjustment categories, actual realization and transaction-date rate inputs, not the accounting multiple.",
          "formula": null,
          "cached_value": null,
          "hidden": false,
          "data_type": null,
          "number_format": null,
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "locator": "line 91",
          "text": "**Debt and lien permissions are separate.** L p.18 §4.09 L1295 says **“greater than 2.0 to 1.0”**, not greater than or equal. L p.10 L715 says **“shall not exceed 5.25 to 1.00”** for the specific (xxxi) Ratio Indebtedness lien route. Permitted Liens (iii) covers Bank Indebtedness; (xx) links purchase-money and additional-debt baskets to asset-specific/collateral-only limits; (xxi) confines foreign-sub liens to foreign-sub assets. Accordingly, 5.25 is not a blanket secured leverage maintenance ceiling or a condition on every lien. Permitted-debt reclassification can refresh fixed baskets; acquisition debt can use an improved-FCCR alternative even without satisfying the USD1 ratio-debt test. These provisions can permit further pari claims or locally senior funding without a new breach, but actual priming is not established. The contrary case is §4.12's express junior-or-permitted requirement and §9.02's affected-holder ranking protection. A proposed priority change must satisfy those boundaries and the missing ICA, rather than relying on a generic majority-vote claim.",
          "formula": null,
          "cached_value": null,
          "hidden": false,
          "data_type": null,
          "number_format": null,
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "locator": "line 93",
          "text": "**Leakage can occur before default and may outlast deteriorating tests.** §4.07 L1265 permits **“any Restricted Payment”** subject to no continuing Default/EoD and pro forma FCCR exceeding 2.0x. L1272 preserves certain payments contractually committed while conditions held. The builder basket therefore is not the sole potential distribution constraint. Permitted Investments can reach non-guarantors, and designation of a guarantor as Unrestricted can release its guarantee and liens under §§10.07(c),12.07(f), subject to designation and RP conditions. Asset-sale exclusions, §5.01's intragroup carveout and affiliate carveouts mean a transfer may avoid one covenant yet remain subject to others. No categorical IP-transfer prohibition is identified in the supplied indenture; this is a conditional route, not a finding that material IP has been transferred. Without an entity/IP schedule, valuation and usage ledger its amount is Not calculable. These mechanics can reduce creditors' reachable value without an immediate payment default; monitor designations, intragroup transfers, RP commitments and releases as well as reported dividends.",
          "formula": null,
