        {
          "locator": "line 97",
          "text": "**Asset-sale protection is real but delayed and qualified.** FMV consideration and conditional cash requirements, reinvestment/application deadlines, and a pro rata 100%-plus-interest offer protect noteholders where §4.10 applies. Countervailing flexibility includes deemed cash (assumed liabilities, instruments converted within 180 days and designated noncash consideration), long reinvestment periods, net-proceeds deductions, use to repay secured or non-guarantor debt, and return of untendered residual to permitted general purposes. The special productive-assets alternative requires substitute Productive Assets promptly to become Collateral where sold assets were collateral (L1317). This supports collateral continuity in that path, but is not a universal requirement that all proceeds immediately repay these Notes. Do not collapse asset-sales proceeds into near-term note amortization.",
