        {
          "locator": "line 99",
          "text": "**Guarantees improve direct recourse but are neither universal nor permanent.** §10.01 promises unconditional, irrevocable, joint-and-several payment/performance, not merely collection, with reinstatement for rescinded payments; §10.02 limits enforceability by fraudulent-transfer law. The executed signer list includes CPI, Calspan, Raptor entities and TransDigm UK, among others (L pp.31–32), but is not a current exhaustive ownership/value schedule. §4.17's facility limb and separate >=200 capital-markets limb can capture new obligors, with 20-Business-Day accession; §12.04 links required guarantee accession to security/ICA joinder. §10.07 nonetheless releases on permitted external disposals, compliant USub designation, immateriality under its conditions, release from specified triggering debt, or funded discharge/defeasance. Immaterial Domestic Restricted Subsidiary requires both <=2.5% EBITDA and <=2.5% assets, using the specified >45-day reporting lag (L p.7 L535); no aggregate immateriality cap is stated in that definition. A non-guarantor is not the same as an Unrestricted Subsidiary, and a foreign subsidiary is not automatically outside every guarantee: TransDigm UK is expressly excluded from the defined Foreign Restricted Subsidiary category and signs here.",
