          "note": null
        },
        {
          "locator": "line 101",
          "text": "**Security documentation determines realized control.** Collateral excludes the absent Security Agreement's Excluded Collateral (L p.4 L389). §12.03 conditions some further collateralization on corresponding facility requirements; §12.06 provides commercially reasonable perfection efforts and a 90-day outside period, not evidence those filings were completed. §12.07(e)(B) follows specified Credit Agreement Collateral Agent releases, but excludes the stated full-cash facility discharge outside foreclosure/remedies; it is not an automatic release whenever the facility is repaid. §12.07(e)(A) can release collateral transferred outside Company/Holdings/Guarantors in a permitted transaction, potentially including a restricted non-guarantor recipient, subject to full operative conditions. Permitted automatic releases differ from amendments releasing substantially all collateral outside the documents. Certificates and opinions are required to evidence requested releases; none is supplied here.",
