        },
        {
          "locator": "line 134",
          "text": "CP-4's operative findings are material to this comparison: any-RP permission requires no continuing Default/EoD and pro forma legal FCCR **exceeding 2.0x**; permitted commitments may survive later deterioration. Debt permission and lien permission are separate; the **5.25x** secured net ratio belongs to a specific permitted-lien route, not a universal maintenance cap. Projected savings and other legal adjustments can expand transaction capacity without contemporaneous realized cash. These are CP-4 F02–F07 interpretations, not tests computed from CP-1's 4,173 EBITDA As Defined or 6,261 cash. Actual unused baskets, elections, legal EBITDA, eligible cash and the September dividend route remain Not calculable.",
