          "number_format": null,
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "locator": "line 136",
          "text": "Counterprotection matters. General majority amendment does **not** establish an unrestricted majority priming right: L §9.02 protects adversely changed ranking/payment terms for affected holders and requires 66⅔% for specified nonpermitted sweeping collateral release or materially adverse ICA modification (pp.26–27, L1834–L1860). Conversely, permitted releases under §§10.07/12.07 do not necessarily need a new vote. Holders cannot directly enforce Security Documents individually or collectively; agents act under documents and the ICA, which controls conflicts (L pp.29–31, §§11.16,12.01,12.02,12.08). Missing operative ICA standstill, turnover, control votes and purchase options prevent a complete timing/waterfall conclusion. No actual coercive LME, uptier, drop-down, default or perfection failure is established.",
