          "note": null
        },
        {
          "locator": "line 144",
          "text": "### Downside, loss mechanisms and strongest countercases",
          "formula": null,
          "cached_value": null,
          "hidden": false,
          "data_type": null,
          "number_format": null,
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "locator": "line 146",
          "text": "**Time-aware operating downside:** from the September 2024 base, weaker utilization or qualified-supplier disruption first reduces spares demand or deliverable shipments (CP-1A B10/B11/B14), then revenue/mix and margin (B04/B08), then collections and inventory conversion (B13; CP-1 K03). Interest, reinvestment and committed payouts compete for cash. Borrowing may initially bridge cash needs but raises claims; eligible A/R may tighten just when liquidity is needed. A July 2025 renewal requirement can matter before longer bond maturities, but no outcome is inferred from the missing follow-up. Notes need not suffer an immediate numerical maintenance breach simply because earnings fall. Transaction incurrence/RP permissions, payment default rules and refinancing access are distinct pathways (CP-4 F01/F13).",
          "formula": null,
          "cached_value": null,
          "hidden": false,
          "data_type": null,
          "number_format": null,
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "locator": "line 148",
          "text": "**Economic loss versus legal loss:** spread widening or rates rising can create mark-to-market loss before any default. Fixed longer notes face duration plus credit-spread repricing; floating loans can have less fixed-rate duration but credit discount and exit-liquidity risk, while higher floating service costs affect issuer cash. In a later restructuring, lower enterprise/pool values, senior dilution, leakage, costs and realization delay reduce distributable proceeds; subordination makes juniors more convex to residual shortfall. A bond's par shortfall is not the investor's entry-price loss: economic loss depends on purchase price, proceeds, interim cash and timing, all of which are missing here. No assumed recovery floor, stress magnitude, PD or portfolio loss is assigned.",
          "formula": null,
          "cached_value": null,
          "hidden": false,
          "data_type": null,
          "number_format": null,
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "locator": "line 150",
          "text": "**Economic countercase:** installed-base replacement demand, improving historical conversion and completed extensions may allow retained cash to reduce refinancing dependence. It would win if subsequent comparable financial evidence showed recurring conversion after maintenance/integration needs, actual debt retirement and restrained discretionary payouts. That would improve all claims, potentially letting discounted subordinated debt outperform on price; it still needs verified compensation and residual support.",
          "formula": null,
          "cached_value": null,
          "hidden": false,
          "data_type": null,
          "number_format": null,
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "locator": "line 152",
          "text": "**Legal countercase:** guarantees, intended first-priority liens, junior-or-permitted conditions and sacred voting rights may preserve more reachable value than the leakage-risk narrative suggests. It would win if the full executed package, filings, entity map and transaction certificates demonstrate retained collateral, enforceable coverage and constrained competing claims. This would raise conviction in the secured protection case, not mechanically establish its fair spread.",
          "formula": null,
          "cached_value": null,
          "hidden": false,
          "data_type": null,
          "number_format": null,
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "locator": "line 154",
          "text": "**Structural countercase:** a senior label does not ensure superior investment outcome if assets sit in excluded/non-guarantor pools, agents cannot realize value promptly or price already discounts almost no loss. Conversely, enforceable junior guarantees and a sufficiently low entry price could compensate for subordination. Verified entity values, competing claims and comparable prices would decide; missing documents do not prove the adverse structural case. These countercases keep structural preference conditional and implementation withheld rather than converting gaps into Avoid decisions.",
