          "note": null
        },
        {
          "locator": "line 160",
          "text": "Conditionally, floating secured exposure could suit a vehicle seeking floating income and verified senior asset reach, but it adds rate-service sensitivity, repricing/assignment and liquidity issues. Fixed secured bonds could suit a duration-bearing mandate with sufficient spread compensation and tolerance for call asymmetry. Subordinated exposure requires a mandate able to bear residual-value loss and price volatility, as well as evidence that compensation pays for those risks. Aerospace/defense, issuer, bank/loan and fixed-duration concentrations would have to be measured jointly with existing holdings; reporting segments are not independent correlated-risk buckets. No such category is declared suitable for this unspecified portfolio.",
