          "text": "The committee selects **Requires More Work**. Neither side establishes an implementable investment: the Bull supports improving historical operating cash and meaningful contractual protections, while the Bear establishes that actual extraction and conditional legal flexibility can keep that cash from becoming a creditor cushion. The Bear does not prove a liquidity failure, an unlawful payment or an inevitable restructuring. The decisive distinction is between operating capacity and retained, accessible resources. With neither a complete liquidity/downside bridge nor executable prices and portfolio evidence, a Starter Position would convert a plausible credit thesis into unsupported clearance. Avoid would likewise overstate the evidence by treating absent compensation and liquidity proof as demonstrated inadequacy. The conclusion preserves CP-3's Requires More Work/RV Unclear posture and CP-5's Restricted historical-use boundary.",
