          "text": "Function 8: **Neither wins** under the method's winner definitions. Bull wins a bounded historical conversion proposition; Bear wins the cash-retention/policy objection, but cannot prove that downside overwhelms all mitigants. The Zero-Bound chain is a credible conditional mechanism, not a proved exhaustion path: shock magnitude, accessible starting resources, forecast response and funding outcomes are missing. Accordingly, its guardrail bars a high-conviction long without manufacturing an Avoid decision. The default Starter Position for proven cash durability, accessible liquidity, manageable maturities and fair-to-cheap RV does not apply: the latter three conditions have not been jointly established. Requires More Work is selected instead of Watchlist because usable liquidity, priced selection and portfolio implementation all remain decision-gating, not simply catalyst timing.",
