        {
          "locator": "line 92",
          "text": "**B1 — Improved conversion is a real debt-service mitigant.** Evidence: CP-1 CF22/K02/K12 and CP-2 show annual CFO and pre-acquisition/distribution CFO less capex rising in FY2022–FY2024; conversion to EBITDA As Defined improves. CP-1A B03/B04 supplies management's installed-base/aftermarket rationale, not contracted recurring revenue. Mechanic: repeat replacement consumption plus demonstrated collections and modest historical cash capex can fund interest and reinvestment before discretionary allocation. Credit implication: **Neutral — Stable**, for the historical servicing base, not Positive — Deleveraging. Monitoring: invalidate the durability inference if like-for-like margins cease converting to cash, inventory/receivables absorb more resources, or maintenance/integration needs consume the apparent surplus. Basis: S1 pp.4,109,142; CP-1 definitions retained.",
