          "text": "**B2 — The 2033 package contains meaningful barriers to an overt adverse rewrite.** Evidence: L §10.01 joint-and-several payment guarantees; §9.02 affected-holder principal/payment/ranking protection and 66⅔% for specified nonpermitted substantially-all collateral releases or materially adverse ICA changes; CP-4 F05 also identifies a junior-or-Permitted-Lien condition. Mechanic: direct recourse and class/affected-holder consents constrain an unconstrained majority priority rewrite, increasing the importance of enforcing actual contractual boundaries. Credit implication: **Neutral — Stable**, conditional legal protection, not a recovery floor. Monitoring: new release/designation, secured issuance, consent or ICA change; test actual terms, filings and entity reach rather than infer them from consolidated accounts. Basis: L pp.26–27 §§9.02/10.01; CP-4 F05/F10/F14.",
