          "text": "**Bear Zero-Bound attempt:** From the September 2024 base, weaker utilization, OEM disruption or a qualified-supplier interruption first reduces spares orders/deliverable shipments (CP-1A B10/B11/B14), then adverse mix and costs reduce operating earnings; slower receivables and excess inventory weaken CFO (CP-1 K03; CP-2 downside chain). Interest, reinvestment and committed distributions then compete for accessible resources. Additional borrowing could sustain operations while raising leverage; reduced receivable eligibility or an unrenewed facility could intensify refinancing pressure before the note bullets. Eventually a missed payment or qualifying cross-default could engage CP-4's actual notice/grace/remedy rules. Observable signals are orders/shipments, collection/inventory cash use, declared commitments, eligibility/renewal evidence and formal default notices. **The chain cannot be completed to exhaustion, breach, default timing or investor loss:** the shock magnitude, cost response, accessible starting cash, complete cash bridge, live facilities, valuation and entry price are Not supplied. CP-2A/CP-2D/CP-3C have not been silently executed.",
