        {
          "locator": "line 153",
          "text": "**Decision: Requires More Work; winner: Neither wins.** The strongest Bull evidence is actual improving annual operating cash conversion, not an assumed acquisition synergy or forecast. The strongest Bear evidence is the explicitly debt-funded distribution: stronger operations did not ensure retained creditor resources. Legal/recovery view: direct payment guarantees, affected-holder rights and specified supermajority barriers matter, but conditional permissions/releases, absent full ICA/security evidence and unallocated asset values preclude complete protection or recovery claims. Liquidity/refinancing view: historical tenor extensions and reported maturities are supported; accessible runway and future execution are Insufficient Information. RV/portfolio view: CP-3 remains RV Unclear/Requires More Work; no security or size is approved. Before increasing conviction, obtain the accessible liquidity bridge, material CP-5 scope/chronology resolutions, transaction-level legal evidence, executable comparable prices and actual mandate/holdings. The favorable alternative wins only if recurring conversion becomes retained cash, protection is verified and compensation is adequate—not because missing evidence is interpreted optimistically.",
