        },
        {
          "locator": "line 102",
          "text": "FY2024 operating results improved from FY2023: reported revenue increased from USD 6,585 million to USD 7,940 million, and operating income from USD 2,923 million to USD 3,531 million (CP-1 IS01/IS06; S1 p.106). The checked CP-1 K13 deltas are USD 1,355 million and USD 608 million, respectively. EBITDA As Defined increased from USD 3,395 million to USD 4,173 million, while its calculated margin fraction increased from 0.515566 to 0.525567 (SG16/K06). This establishes historical earnings progress, not a verified organic or price-led bridge. CP-1A X01/X02 documents acquisitions in the same period; their full-year contribution and realized integration returns are not established.",
          "formula": null,
          "cached_value": null,
          "hidden": false,
          "data_type": null,
          "number_format": null,
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "locator": "line 104",
          "text": "Operating cash increased from USD 1,375 million to USD 2,045 million; CP-1 calculated CFO less signed capex increased from USD 1,236 million to USD 1,880 million (CF22/CF23/K02). Conversion to EBITDA As Defined improved from 0.405007 to 0.490055 (K12). The complete annual assets/liabilities cash effect remained negative, at USD (431) million in FY2023 and USD (302) million in FY2024 (K03). Improvement therefore coexisted with continuing cash absorption, and unresolved cash-bridge scope differences prevent collapsing all change measures into one working-capital definition.",
          "formula": null,
