          "hidden": false,
          "data_type": null,
          "number_format": null,
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "locator": "line 106",
          "text": "The financing comparison is less favorable for retention. Carrying debt increased from USD 19,750 million to USD 24,880 million, and carrying debt/EBITDA As Defined increased from 5.817378 to 5.962138 multiples (K07/K09). Cash rose from USD 3,472 million to USD 6,261 million, producing a lower mechanical cash-netted ratio, but FY2024 ended with USD 4,216 million of dividends payable (BS01/BS14/K10). CP-1A BF01 supplies the direct debt-funded distribution link; X06 supplies the countervailing history of successful extensions. October payments are subsequent events, not FY2024 cash outflows. These observations explain why improved operations and a larger cash balance do not establish deleveraging or a permanently stronger liquidity buffer.",
